#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096406 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "28008aa6-6be6-52dd-9459-097113538b13" :question/math-academy-id "e-501" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)-1 & =A(-2-3)+B(-2+2) \\\\ -5 & =A(-5)+B(0) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)-1 & =A(3-3)+B(3+2) \\\\ 5 & =A(0)+B(5) \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096410 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "d10d11a8-6a30-59b6-bb0e-6065e60bbc6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-502" :question/problem "Express $\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+5(-2)+7 & =A(-2-3)(-2+1) \\\\ 5 & =A(5) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)^{2}+5(3)+7 & =B(3+2)(3+1) \\\\ 40 & =B(20) \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}+5(-1)+7 & =C(-1+2)(-1-3) \\\\ 4 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1,$ $B=2,$ and $C=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289074 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77fa05a0-065f-55e0-8772-10a5bc27239c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289076} {:answer/id #uuid "6a91d886-93d0-55d4-8332-e22191fabdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289077} {:answer/id #uuid "20089555-b2b4-5881-a546-c245548b5d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289078} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f0d6d2-2f1c-5b64-ac9e-f8c29191a81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289079} {:answer/id #uuid "74990dcd-b63e-5bb8-9b9e-0d439fcabe1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1f0d6d2-2f1c-5b64-ac9e-f8c29191a81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289079} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbf946a-6bde-519f-b590-8ddb36f996c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49eb189d-dbb6-571c-b92b-059f64da6668" :question/math-academy-id "q-10972" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n6x-25=A(x+5)+B(x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)-25 & =A(0+5)+B(0) \\\\ -25 & =5A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{25}{5} \\\\ A & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(-5)-25 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5) \\\\ -55 & =-5B \\\\ B & =\\frac{-55}{-5} \\\\ B & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-5+11=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} {:answer/id #uuid "3d30d3f4-7110-5d7a-94f1-05de257882c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255562} {:answer/id #uuid "db33c0c3-efd2-5101-8afc-0e00d60594ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255563} {:answer/id #uuid "3e25788b-7544-5f2b-9242-937076aff43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255564} {:answer/id #uuid "c348aa84-f04d-5685-8e7d-055cf33fe3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c323c9-b4b7-55de-b8fb-b1fc59ed12ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255561} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4fc8d6-5aac-5a3d-a9b2-82befae980c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca8ed292-7934-54b0-b0fb-7d888622b0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-10974" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-3x)(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n7x-37=A(2x+3)+B(5-3x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-\\frac{3}{2})-37 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(5-3(-\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\ \\frac{-21-74}{2} & =B(\\frac{10+9}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{-95}{2} & =B(\\frac{19}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-95}{19} \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(\\frac{5}{3})-37 & =A(2(\\frac{5}{3})+3)+B(5-3(\\frac{5}{3})) \\\\ \\frac{35-111}{3} & =A(\\frac{10+9}{3}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-76}{19} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be68e142-9d17-56e3-848c-1b72b082a31c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6)/((2x + 1)) + (2)/((x + 5)) - (11)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093592} {:answer/id #uuid "1f757042-e4a1-554d-b16d-4da22ea8f9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1)/((2x + 1)) + (3)/((x + 5)) - (2)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093593} {:answer/id #uuid "345ef20a-3f1b-5298-9488-3f854c9abd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/((2x + 1)) + (4)/((x + 5)) + (5)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093594} {:answer/id #uuid "4b402463-0065-51ea-8fca-7d152a65bf58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (1)/((2x + 1)) + (6)/((x + 5)) - (3)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093595} {:answer/id #uuid "53acb89b-cf3f-53bc-8174-ab692ea114e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (4)/((2x + 1)) + (7)/((x + 5)) + (4)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "345ef20a-3f1b-5298-9488-3f854c9abd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (2)/((2x + 1)) + (4)/((x + 5)) + (5)/((x + 1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093594} :answer-field/id #uuid "589432c7-1073-5e41-9823-b0fe65045453" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c52ae0a6-ddb7-585f-9b74-6be345d63c9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-10981" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n16{x}^{2}+55x+19=A(x+5)(x+1)+B(2x+1)(x+1)+C(2x+1)(x+5).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+55(-\\frac{1}{2})+19 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+5)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+5) \\\\ 4-\\frac{55}{2}+19 & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{46-55}{2} & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-36}{18} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-5)^{2}+55(-5)+19 & =A(-5+5)(-5+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-5)+1)(-5+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-5)+1)(-5+5) \\\\ 400-275+19 & =B((-9)(-4)) \\\\ B & =\\frac{144}{36} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-1)^{2}+55(-1)+19 & =A(-1+5)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-1)+1)(-1+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-1)+1)(-1+5) \\\\ 16-55+19 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-4} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}=-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c326bf8e-2b8b-5dd6-b7d2-52577291f94c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4)/((x + 1)) - (6)/((2 - x)) - (7)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093598} {:answer/id #uuid "d264dacd-baf6-5b64-99d4-570051c1e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) + (5)/((2 - x)) + (4)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093599} {:answer/id #uuid "e289503f-8c52-5b9f-acec-676b54e03fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8)/((x + 1)) + (1)/((2 - x)) + (2)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093600} {:answer/id #uuid "61c5bf61-37b5-542a-92f5-fc05b1823fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) - (2)/((2 - x)) + (6)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093601} {:answer/id #uuid "71d5bdac-5ec1-5d38-8f77-e8b38ecb7437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2)/((x + 1)) - (1)/((2 - x)) - (3)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d264dacd-baf6-5b64-99d4-570051c1e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3)/((x + 1)) + (5)/((2 - x)) + (4)/((x + 3))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093599} :answer-field/id #uuid "52353003-cdba-5f9b-aa22-71bc1949607f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea90bdf7-7ef9-5956-892d-81c701801ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-10989" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+1)}+\\frac{B}{(2-x)}+\\frac{C}{(x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+21x+41=A(2-x)(x+3)+B(x+1)(x+3)+C(x+1)(2-x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+21(-1)+41 & =A(2-(-1))(-1+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-1+1)(-1+3) \\\\  & +C(-1+1)(2-(-1)) \\\\ -2-21+41 & =A(6) \\\\ A & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+21(2)+41 & =A(2-2)(2+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(2+1)(2+3) \\\\  & +C(2+1)(2-2) \\\\ -8+42+41 & =B(15) \\\\ B & =\\frac{75}{15} \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-3)^{2}+21(-3)+41 & =A(2-(-3))(-3+3) \\\\  & \\,+B(-3+1)(-3+3) \\\\  & +C(-3+1)(2-(-3)) \\\\ -18-63+41 & =C(-10) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-40}{-10} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+21x+41}{(x+1)(2-x)(x+3)}=\\frac{3}{(x+1)}+\\frac{5}{(2-x)}+\\frac{4}{(x+3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289089 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df797e27-a173-5b04-9f46-8d090078f38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df797e27-a173-5b04-9f46-8d090078f38e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289091} :answer-field/id #uuid "92430816-e191-55f5-a35c-fd2663b67f23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbf7949e-794d-58c7-ac2f-19452bc80c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-350930" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n|  | $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,=\\,\\frac{2}{x-3}\\,\\,+$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2x+1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+5=2(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-\\frac{1}{2})+5 & =2(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{-1}{2x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c750b503-d761-5306-9a48-199a0a56b4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c750b503-d761-5306-9a48-199a0a56b4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299285} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ac06ac1-0ed5-5d6c-a4da-a335243c819e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5c75d54-5a8a-5074-ad31-4334e1979979" :question/math-academy-id "q-350934" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+1$ |  | $x+3$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n5x+11=A(x+3)+2(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-1)+11 & =A(-1+3)+2(-1+1) \\\\ 6 & =2A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+11}{(x+1)(x+3)}=\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{x+3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "450aebfe-d896-50bc-a392-e43aee7afabd" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Two Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af1258a6-8a9f-5108-955d-fb5228710cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299288} {:answer/id #uuid "11f58b7f-9636-5b63-ad91-203ed10257e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af1258a6-8a9f-5108-955d-fb5228710cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299288} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43d5216-bdea-5199-98d0-80b683f15a24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bd503f3-e108-5605-a285-fe505d0132b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bd503f3-e108-5605-a285-fe505d0132b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299291} :answer-field/id #uuid "7113323a-e369-532c-89f4-ae7e995aa587" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8a64fcd-2ae3-54d6-ab3a-f736d8506ae6" :question/math-academy-id "q-350940" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x$ |  | $x-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n4-5x=A(x-1)+Bx.\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-5(0) & =A(0-1)+B(0) \\\\ 4 & =-A \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-5(1) & =A(1-1)+B(1) \\\\ -1 & =B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5x}{x(x-1)}=\\frac{-4}{x}+\\frac{-1}{x-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c22605db-cac2-5f94-a4d4-efb7e6ccde60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22605db-cac2-5f94-a4d4-efb7e6ccde60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299294} :answer-field/id #uuid "22a4fbed-f5e0-555a-bdb7-17286fb56373" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299293} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "278fa2c3-0329-5131-a0f1-b1d31436680f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "278fa2c3-0329-5131-a0f1-b1d31436680f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299296} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e6cec30-eea3-56fe-80a6-984171756381" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ea2a58-8b1e-5d43-aab8-a144acbd6833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ea2a58-8b1e-5d43-aab8-a144acbd6833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299298} :answer-field/id #uuid "976ab995-8544-573b-95bb-64062fc38295" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06babcd4-bbb4-5621-bb1f-d33fa0f96d00" :question/math-academy-id "q-350968" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-2$ |  | $x+1$ |  | $3x+4$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{x+1}+\\frac{C}{3x+4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+19x+30=A(x+1)(3x+4)+B(x-2)(3x+4)+C(x-2)(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(2)^{2}+19(2)+30 & =A(2+1)(3(2)+4)+B(2-2)(3(2)+4)+C(2-2)(2+1) \\\\ 60 & =30A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+19(-1)+30 & =A(-1+1)(3(-1)+4)+B(-1-2)(3(-1)+4)+C(-1-2)(-1+1) \\\\ 9 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{4}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}+19(-\\frac{4}{3})+30 & =A(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+B(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(3(-\\frac{4}{3})+4) \\\\  & \\,\\,+C(-\\frac{4}{3}-2)(-\\frac{4}{3}+1) \\\\ \\frac{10}{9} & =\\frac{10}{9}C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+19x+30}{(x-2)(x+1)(3x+4)}=\\frac{2}{x-2}-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{1}{3x+4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9df0cbe6-3751-5c6f-b437-9d62124b3bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9df0cbe6-3751-5c6f-b437-9d62124b3bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299301} :answer-field/id #uuid "861df757-d51b-59b9-98cb-e060221974ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299300} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34310332-fd54-5749-8b6f-d5a6212339ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34310332-fd54-5749-8b6f-d5a6212339ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299303} :answer-field/id #uuid "620ec75e-9986-557c-be41-110ca7dd7d1b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81425749-b638-5f9c-bd20-e55d0ec93a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81425749-b638-5f9c-bd20-e55d0ec93a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299305} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b65804c-836c-5633-b753-a23cc13ed14f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4f3ed87d-5ab6-56a5-bf4e-dbbffa2cf3fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-351007" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2x+1$ |  | $3x-4$ |  | $x-2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{3x-4}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n18-19x=A(3x-4)(x-2)+B(2x+1)(x-2)+C(2x+1)(3x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =A(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4) \\\\ \\frac{55}{2} & =\\frac{55}{4}A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{4}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(\\frac{4}{3}) & =A(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4) \\\\ -\\frac{22}{3} & =-\\frac{22}{9}B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(2) & =A(3(2)-4)(2-2)+B(2(2)+1)(2-2)+C(2(2)+1)(3(2)-4) \\\\ -20 & =10C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\frac{3}{3x-4}-\\frac{2}{x-2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e66d7cf-1a4b-51e6-9c78-f70a8c0555df" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Rational Function With Three Linear Factors as a Sum of Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b30ba91-ae46-5c8a-a706-eadf49473929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268294} {:answer/id #uuid "5487de66-7dc7-5034-8054-c95e685f72e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{4}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268295} {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} {:answer/id #uuid "b551016b-e3f4-554b-afb5-1871fb7b2e49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268297} {:answer/id #uuid "39114682-6ec7-594e-8ef7-e381555c6285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf3373e-14ce-53af-958f-71db5e3cd93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268296} :answer-field/id #uuid "22269ea3-ba61-5af1-b9c9-78ad9e0d52ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e23b9540-6b27-5f85-a262-32ee244fff8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-69751" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n12x+12=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-3)(x+5)+C(x-3)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(3)+12 & =A(3-1)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3-3)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3-3)(3-1) \\\\ 36+12 & =A(2)(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{48}{16} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1)+12 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-3)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-3)(1-1) \\\\ 12+12 & =B(-2)(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{24}{-12} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(-5)+12 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-3)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-3)(-5-1) \\\\ -60+12 & =C(-8)(-6) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-48}{48} \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}.\n$$"}]}
